<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CLICKING A TAKE LANE MUST COMP THAT TAKE ON A **WRAPPED** COLUMN — and the
  new take must be HEARD, not merely highlighted.

  THE SHAPE. A take column reaches a track two ways: DIRECT
  (`SLink -> STakeStack`, what add-take builds) and WRAPPED
  (`SLink -> SCut -> STakeStack`, what a SHARED or PLACED column is). Only the
  direct one had a gate — take_lane_click_split.qxa. A real saved project
  carries the wrapped one, and on it the comping gesture did NOTHING AT ALL.

  THREE DEFECTS, all on this one gesture, each found only because the one
  before it was fixed:

    1. `SSelectTakeAction::apply` resolved its stack with a bare
       `dynamic_cast<STakeStack*>( &link->getSObject() )`, true only of the
       DIRECT shape. On the wrapped shape the link's object is the WRAPPER, so
       the action was REFUSED and the click did nothing. (The take-lane UI has
       always unwrapped — SMVActualView's takeStackOfLink — so the gesture the
       UI could express was one the action would not accept.)
    2. With that fixed the model changed and the AUDIO did not.
       `STakeStack::setActiveTake` publishes through `durationChanged`, which
       on the direct shape the TRACK is connected to (`twTrackMix::updateClip`
       -> a content-epoch bump and a state-chain reset, plus the range
       invalidation). On the wrapped shape the link's object is the WINDOW,
       and a window does not listen to its content's `durationChanged`: that
       emission had NO listener. `stakes::publishColumnChange` republishes the
       window's own unchanged duration, which is exactly what the track's slot
       needs. Dropping the wrapper's capture and staling its render path were
       BOTH tried and are NOT substitutes — measured.
    3. A RACE, and it is why this case renders BEFORE the click as well as
       after. `SCut::buildCapture_` runs on a revalidator worker holding only
       `captureBuildMutex_`, which deliberately does not exclude
       `invalidateCapture()`. Measured: a worker entered the build and
       resolved the stack at take 0; the click set take 1 and invalidated in
       the SAME millisecond; the worker published its take-0 capture 2 ms
       later, over the invalidation; the next render served it. `captureGen_`
       makes the invalidation win. A case that only renders AFTER the click
       cannot see this — the capture would be cold and correct.

  THE FIXTURE IS A CLOSED FORM. takestack_wrap_takeslip.qxp puts a 2 s wrapper
  window 2 s into the stack (`srcStart='96000'`) over test_gapsaw.wav — a
  0.1 -> 0.8 amplitude ramp with EXACT-ZERO regions at [0.6,0.9) and
  [2.5,3.0) s. take 0 is slipped half a second in (`srcStart='24000'`), take 1
  is not. A sawtooth of amplitude A has RMS A/sqrt(3), so each half-second
  window is arithmetic, not a measurement:

      take 0 (active on load) -> source [2.5,4.5) -> 0 / 0.38638 / 0.43686 / 0
      take 1 (clicked here)   -> source [2.0,4.0) -> 0.28544 / 0 / 0.38638 / 0.43686

  The two disagree in EVERY window, and the first two swap outright, so no
  window can pass by accident.

  ROWS. `set-lane-view toggleTakesRow="0"` expands track1's take lanes:
  row 0 = track1's composite lane, row 1 = take 0's lane, row 2 = take 1's
  lane, row 3 = the sentinel track2. The click is `drag-clip-edge` with
  `toTime` AT the clip's own body midpoint (48000 = 1 s of a 2 s clip at 0),
  i.e. zero pixel movement — a press and release at one point, which is what
  take_lane_click_split.qxa uses too.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="take_lane_click_wrapped">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <load-project path="../takestack_wrap_takeslip.qxp"/>

    <!-- BEFORE: take 0 is active on load. This render is not decoration —
         it is what makes defect 3 above reachable (it warms the capture and
         starts the revalidator traffic the click then has to beat). -->
    <render filename="tlcw_before.wav" format="wav" quality="10"
            durationSec="2.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tlcw_before.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.002"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tlcw_before.wav"
                         startFrame="24000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.380" maxRms="0.392"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tlcw_before.wav"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.430" maxRms="0.443"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tlcw_before.wav"
                         startFrame="72000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.002"/>

    <set-lane-view toggleTakesRow="0"/>

    <!-- THE GESTURE: a plain left click on TAKE 1's lane row. Before defect 1
         was fixed the nested SSelectTakeAction was REJECTED, and the runner
         (which counts the global rejection counter) fails the enclosing
         drag-clip-edge outright — so this line alone is the defect-1 gate. -->
    <drag-clip-edge track="2" clip="0" edge="body" toTime="48000"/>

    <!-- AFTER: take 1's window, in the SAME process, over pages and a capture
         that are all still resident. Every window differs from the four
         above; windows 1 and 2 swap loud for silent. -->
    <render filename="tlcw_after.wav" format="wav" quality="10"
            durationSec="2.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tlcw_after.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.280" maxRms="0.291"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tlcw_after.wav"
                         startFrame="24000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.002"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tlcw_after.wav"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.380" maxRms="0.392"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tlcw_after.wav"
                         startFrame="72000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.430" maxRms="0.443"/>

    <!-- The click comps the column; it does not MOVE or RESIZE it. -->
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="0" duration="96000"
                        startOffset="96000"/>
  </actions>

</SActionScript>
